		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="1034"></a><b>meneltel</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Praefectus Castrorum<br /><br /><br />Joined: 02 Mar 2003<br />Posts: 157<br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=1034&amp;sid=b16eca86cb9e28f404298759615589f6#1034"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Wed Jun 25, 2003 10:39 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: Revenge</span></td>
				<td valign="top" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=1034&amp;sid=b16eca86cb9e28f404298759615589f6"><img src="templates/smartDark/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Meneltel stormed through the new home of Domus Noctis with all her rage and anger apparent across her dark but pretty face even though now the beauty was gone and anger was present.  The guards stood to attention afraid to be noticed if they left their posts for fear of what she would do to them for failing to do their duties.
<br />
     "Guard Captain X'Lotto, front and center......NOW!" screamed Meneltel with all the hatred of Innoruuk in her voice.  She stood impatiently for a few seconds before heading to the guard captain's post only to run into him as he rushed around a corner heading to her at her command.  He bounced off of her and fell back onto the floor and then scrambled to his feet to stand at attention.  "Guard Captain X'Lotto; present at your request, Battlemistress."  He saluted her and did his best not to notice her anger being directed at him.
<br />
     "Captain X'Lotto, did I not instruct you that no, I repeat NO ONE was to enter my room while I was away?" Meneltel all but screamed at him.
<br />
The handsome Dark elf captain replied nervously, "That was your orders, Battlemistress, and no one...".  "Silence, fool", snapped Meneltel to him, "for some one HAS been in my room, and stolen a lock of the Demon's hair.  Remember the demon you heard the reports about?" inquired Meneltel. "The one that slaughtered the Felwithe guards? And no comments about how they are only High Elves....I have tasted their blades and magics where you have not."
<br />
     "I had sent a message to the head of the guild that I had taked a lock of Cemberfrost's hair before the trouble all started once i realized that he was being influenced by a demon and I put that lock of hair away for safekeeping....now it is gone....and YOU are responsible for the security of this building, are you not?" asked Meneltel calmly now....too calmly for the guard captain's feelings.
<br />
     "Yes, I am, Battlemistress.  And I serve at yours and Innoruuk's will." he replies after taking a breath of air for courage.  "True", said Meneltel' " but you no longer serve me.  I dismiss you from service.  You will get your next assignment from Innoruuk Himself" she told him as she lifted her hand as it began to glow and touched his chest with it.  He screamed in pain and stumbled back and began to draw his sword when she ordered the guards to kill him.
<br />
     She turned away even as the guards began to attack the doomed captain and headed to her room.  "Who has entered the city who might know about the hair and also had the power to enter my room?" Meneltel wondered, ignoring the screams of pain and combat from behind her as it echoed through the building.  "Not many know where we moved the Noctis headquarters to and it was recently.  So only someone in the guild or familiar with Neriak might know."
<br />
     She reached her room and entered it and sat down on her arm chair luxuriating in the feel of the chair, knowing she skinned the elven slaves in Crushbone, stripping the skin off of their arms and leaving them alive to work still in the orcish mines.  "Who could make use of the hair and had knowledge of it and of the city?  The Spurned? They have the magical skills but would not dare cross me and the guards and all my allies in the city.  No, it wasnt someone directly in the city as they would have far too much to lose from my wrath and connections.  I must find out who did it."
<br />
     And so begins the search for the missing lock of hair.......<br />_________________<br />Don't fear the darkness, fear what is hidden in the darkness.............                    For your suffering will be legendary........even in Hell</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
